-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-63ee3190-a171-4a3b-8eaa-378a3b4e4e75"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Science/Industry Collaboration : Bugs, Project Barons and Managing Symbiosis","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-453189","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"I studier af entreprenørskab og innovation har man siden 1990erne vist stor interesse for leg som en kilde til organisatorisk kreativitet (Driver 2008). Legen forstås her som et middel til at producere det nye og diskuteres som en strategi for at sikre udvikling af innovative produkter og viden (Hjorth 2005). I denne artikel kaster vi et blik på det ”double bind”, der ofte karakteriserer analyser af leg, hvad enten de foretages i udviklingspsykologien, antropologien eller i litteraturen om entreprenørskab og innovation. På den ene side er leg blevet interessant som forskningsobjekt, fordi den antages at rumme muligheder for nyskabelse og hjælper os med at tænke friere og helt ud af boksen. På den anden side synes de eksisterende analyser af leg i forskellige discipliner at udgrænse netop disse præmisser. Netop det som fascinerede i første omgang, det kreative, det uforudsigeligt skabende og det gakkede, bliver det, som må udgrænses for at legen bliver forståelig som forskningsobjekt. I ovennævnte discipliner er tendensen at betragte leg som produktiv, når, og kun når, den foregår i en særlig boble adskilt fra den \"virkelige\" virkelighed, og analytisk er tendensen, at legen må underlægges en målsætning eller et krav om specifikke resultater fra en verden ”uden for” boblen, før den kan opfattes som legitim. Leg bliver således først interessant for analysen, hvis den kan reduceres til noget andet end ”bare leg”. Fokus flyttes fra selve legens proces til dens formål og funktion for en større kontekst ”udenfor”. I den operation er ideen om nytte ikke til diskussion. Artiklen udfordrer de grundantagelser, der lader til at have været styrende for måden, vi studerer leg på i dag. Vi tager denne udfordring op ved at kigge nærmere på børnehavebørns leg, som synes at undvige enhver målrationalitet. Kan dette perspektiv hjælpe os med at tænke anderledes, når vi studerer leg i andre felter?","author_count":2,"contributors":["Botelho, Flora","Gorm Hansen, Birgitte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-525197"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"midt i legen innovation i børnehøjde","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://tidsskrift.antropologi.ku.dk/kommende_numre/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-525197","ids":["ku-dc91be15-0484-4599-8c09-9f4c0b1630c4"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8B8C29F2347C34CE4E13FE01F7ABFDDA"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology, Department of Anthropology, Study Council"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Flora","key":"botelhopau","last":"Botelho","locid":"d6436094-be14-4d18-959e-b503003d4bf9","name":"Botelho, Flora","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Birgitte","key":"gormhansenpau","last":"Gorm Hansen","locid":"460137fd-102f-48e3-b0f6-2f6a25e4aa8a","name":"Gorm Hansen, Birgitte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09063021"],"issue":"1","journal":"Tidsskriftet Antropologi","pages":"51-67","status":"p","title":"Tidsskriftet Antropologi","volume":"75"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-dc91be15-0484-4599-8c09-9f4c0b1630c4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Midt i legen : Innovation i børnehøjde","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-525197","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Science as a practice is characterised by two types of visibility. On the one hand scientists make nature visible via imaging technologies; on the other hand they make scientific practice visible as relevant and useful to society. The sociology of translation has paved the way for analysing these two types of visibility as intrinsic parts of the same scientific practice but does not take into account the costs of putting science itself under the gaze. Based on ethnographic field work with Nano scientists the paper compares the costs of making nature visible with the costs of making science. Both types of visibility entail a necessary process of manufacturing the object of knowledge in order for it to display 'feelable forces' in relation the gaze through which visibility is obtained. The paper analyses how science acquires double visibility by a process of enhancement and erasure; two operations constitutive of producing visibility.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Gorm Hansen, Birgitte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-443820"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feeling to see oversight in knowledge production","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-443820","ids":["ku-545fce3e-4750-4182-bf4c-7298f1161ead"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-21B53B701020CD02BA4EFCD7B8E1A649"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Birgitte","key":"gormhansenpau","last":"Gorm Hansen","locid":"460137fd-102f-48e3-b0f6-2f6a25e4aa8a","name":"Gorm Hansen, Birgitte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["14781484","17418135"],"issn_org":["14781484"],"issue":"3/4","journal":"International Journal of Management Concepts and Philosophy","pages":"189-207","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Management Concepts and Philosophy","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-545fce3e-4750-4182-bf4c-7298f1161ead"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Feeling to See: Oversight in Knowledge Production","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-443820","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Kommercialiseringen truer den forskningsmæssige mangfoldighed. For når advokaterne sidder med ved bordet, går det kreative samarbejde i stå.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Gorm Hansen, Birgitte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-410523"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"forsknings politik kun de stærkeste overlever","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://videnskab.dk/kultur-samfund/forsknings-politik-kun-de-staerkeste-overlever","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-410523","ids":["ku-1caa2170-2013-4d65-a8e3-c3b54001fc8c"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4409B02376C1105AB6106745A27605A1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Birgitte","key":"gormhansenpau","last":"Gorm Hansen","locid":"460137fd-102f-48e3-b0f6-2f6a25e4aa8a","name":"Gorm Hansen, Birgitte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["1903301X"],"newspaper":"Videnskab.dk","status":"p","title":"Videnskab.dk","title_org":"videnskab.dk"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1caa2170-2013-4d65-a8e3-c3b54001fc8c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Forsknings-politik: Kun de stærkeste overlever","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-410523","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Kvalitet i undervisningen på de videregående uddannelser er virkelig kommet på dagsordenen efter Rigsrevisionens bedømmelse af universiteternes stigende brug af korttidsansatte medarbejdere. Nu skal der flere timer på programmet, og der skal stilles garanti for forskningsbaseret undervisning. Det kan vise sig vanskeligt at gennemskue, hvordan forskningsbaseret undervisning reelt defineres på de forskellige universiteter, men lad det ligge for nu. I den aktuelle debat defineres forskningsbaseret undervisning tilsyneladende som studerendes kontakt med ’rigtige’ fastansatte forskere snarere end eksterne lektorer, undervisningsassistenter og det, der er værre. I respons på rapporten meldte flere universiteter straks ud, at der snart bliver afsat midler til flere faste stillinger. Mens vi venter på Godot, kan vi passende tænke lidt over, hvordan undervisning blev universitets forsømte barn.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Gorm Hansen, Birgitte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-504161"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"forskerbanens blindgyde dagbladet information","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.information.dk/316724","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-504161","ids":["ku-b9846811-305a-45fd-8c73-4c7740e81269"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9F8F51D9CB3BC6D950C4EA4DC2E44468"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Birgitte","key":"gormhansenpau","last":"Gorm Hansen","locid":"460137fd-102f-48e3-b0f6-2f6a25e4aa8a","name":"Gorm Hansen, Birgitte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16022572"],"newspaper":"Information","status":"p","title":"Information","title_org":"Dagbladet Information"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b9846811-305a-45fd-8c73-4c7740e81269"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Forskerbanens blindgyde, Dagbladet Information","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-504161","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The concepts of “socially robust knowledge” and “mode 2 knowledge production” (Nowotny 2003, Gibbons et al. 1994) have migrated from STS into research policy practices. Both STSscholars and policy makers have been known to propomote the idea that the way forward for today’s scientist is to jump from the ivory tower and learn how to create highflying synergies with citizens, corporations and governments. In STS as well as in Danish research policy it has thus been argued that scientists will gain more support and enjoy greater success in their work by “externalizing” their research and adapting their i nterests to the needs of outside actors. However, when studying the concrete strategies of such successful scientists, matters seem a bit more complicated. Based on interviews with a plant biologist working in GMO the paper uses the biological concepts of field participants as the analytical framework for descri bing the complex relationship between academic science and its so called “external” habitat. Although relational skills and adaptability do seem to be at the heart of successful research management, the key to success does not lie with the ability to assimilate to industrial agendas and concerned citizens. By contrast, it is precisely by not becoming dependent on public opini on, political interest or corporate agendas that a group of Danish GMO researchers managed to survive decades of political resistance and scarce resources. The paper makes a comparison between the development of the danish GMO research group and one of their objects of study: A toxic moth capable of adapting to a hostile environment. Insect strategies for survival are not unlike those deployed by the GMO scientists who study them. The paper argues that scientific ecologies respond to policy change in ways that are unpredictable and difficult to control. Few Danish GMO scientists survived the commercializationwave initiated by neoliberal research policy. However, the ones who did seem to have become more or less resistant to policy change s and public opinion. Rather than promoting socially \"robust knowledge\", Danish research policy seems to have helped develop politically and economically \"robust scientists\". Scientific robustness is acquired by way of three strategies: 1) tasting and discriminating between resources so as to avoid funding that erodes academic profiles and push scientists away from their core i nterests, 2) developing a selfsupply of industry interests by becoming entrepreneurs and thus creating their own compliant industry partner and 3) balancing resources within a larger collective of researchers, thus countering changes in the influx of funding caused by shifts in political and industrial intere sts. The paper concludes by stressing the potential danger of policy habitats who have promoted the evolution of robust scientists based on a competitive system where only the fittest survive. Robust scientists, it is argued, have the potential to become a new “invasive species” in the scientific ecosystem and may threaten the bio diversity of academic research.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Gorm Hansen, Birgitte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-406643"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"robust scientists","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-406643","ids":["ku-16211328-c20d-4174-9bb6-4b221f2e86e7"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-717E6EDF889BFFFEA57C9D1BB4F0AF0C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Birgitte","key":"gormhansenpau","last":"Gorm Hansen","locid":"460137fd-102f-48e3-b0f6-2f6a25e4aa8a","name":"Gorm Hansen, Birgitte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-16211328-c20d-4174-9bb6-4b221f2e86e7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Robust Scientists","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-406643","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Purpose - The purpose of this paper is to explore a visual method, snaplog (snapshots and logbooks) from a performativity theory approach. Design/methodology/approach – The paper uses empirical examples from a three-year qualitative research project where snaplogs are used as an experimental method. The paper presents a reading of performativity theory and discusses the performativity of using visual methods in the research process. Findings – The paper concludes that visual methods have a special ability to activate the field in away that avoids preconceived ideas, and creates possibilities to observe the researched phenomenon and how it practices, resists and revoices the questions asked by the researchers. Research limitations/implications – The paper explores and discusses the authors’ experiences and reflections on the positioning and scope of using snaplogs as a visual method. It does not report a systematic evaluation of its implications. Practical implications – Snaplogs offer the researcher the possibility to activate and cooperate with the researched phenomenon. Originality/value – The potential value of the paper is that it offers inspiration to organization researchers looking for innovative/performative research methods.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bramming, Pia","Gorm Hansen, Birgitte","Olesen, Kristian Gylling","Bojesen, Anders"],"cuid":["S03-080.20-028615"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Forskningsmetode","Logs","Management","Non representationalism","Organizational performance","Organizations","Performativity","Photographs","Qualitative Research","Research methods","Teknologiforståelse","Working environment","Written communications"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AU","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"im perfect pictures snaplogs in performativity research","src":["au","kp","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1108/17465641211223465","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-080.20-028615","identifier":[{"id":"84876301590","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-dc00881c-71fe-45ea-9b96-54eafcee27cf","kp-83a31137-8df0-4da2-9d32-b8cb1fce481e","ku-67c70062-24a3-482a-9ad3-ca4baaa7a20b"],"keyword":["Forskningsmetode","Logs","Management","Non-representationalism","Organizational performance","Organizations","Performativity","Photographs","Qualitative research","Research methods","Snaplog","Teknologiforståelse","Visual research methods","Working environment","Written communications"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-FA2919AE808A89A22F3D7AC669AA18BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1108/17465641211223465","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Department of Education - Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","use